{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"6526821da7e5f681","name":"card_event_bridge_too_far","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/CovertOp/events/card_event_bridge_too_far","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"A BRIDGE TOO FAR","text":"At the end of the enemy turn, add a PANZER III-J to the frontline if possible. Otherwise, destroy all units there.","flavorText":"“A bridge too far” is an idiom inspired by Operation Market Garden, which refers to the act of overreaching, made popular by the 1977 movie of the same name. Operation Market Garden was an ambitious Allied attempt to secure key bridges in the Netherlands and open a route into Germany, but it failed due to a combination of factors. The Germans, despite being outnumbered and surprised by the initial airborne landings, were able to regroup and mount a fierce defense. The terrain, with its rivers and canals, hindered the Allied advance and allowed the Germans to concentrate their forces. Furthermore, communication breakdowns and logistical issues hampered the Allies ability to reinforce their paratroopers, who were eventually defeated by the German counterattack at Arnhem. The German defense, and the tactical errors on the Allied side, resulted in a costly defeat and prolonged the war in Europe.","faction":"Germany","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Rare","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_bridge_too_far","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_bridge_too_far_title","SourceString":"A BRIDGE TOO FAR","LocalizedString":"A BRIDGE TOO FAR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_bridge_too_far_text","SourceString":"At the end of the enemy turn, add a PANZER III-J to the frontline if possible. Otherwise, destroy all units there.","LocalizedString":"At the end of the enemy turn, add a PANZER III-J to the frontline if possible. Otherw